WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.730
- No one really liked me, because of,

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.810
because of the old man smell, so I wasn't

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.810
really close to any of the people there.

00:00:06.845 --> 00:00:07.678
(squeaking)

00:00:07.678 --> 00:00:10.261
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.260
I was working on Bernie Mac,

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.160
and Ken Kwapis, the director, came on,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.160
he was a big fan of my
band The Grassroots,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.450
so I heard that he was
doing the show The Office.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.610
I shot my own talking head,

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.970
presented it to Greg Daniels,

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.340
and they gave me the Halloween episode

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.550
with Steve Carell and
the rest, as they say,

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:32.443
in the books.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.480
Because it's such a great name.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:42.740
I trolled.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.250
Did a lot of trolling for people

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.850
who didn't really want me there.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.430
The character guy, he's in the fray,

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.740
he says, "I can't believe he's making

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.380
"all that music with just his mouth."

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.610
I went in the other
room with the director,

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.700
I says, "why don't you just

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.253
"come on close to me
and, you don't have to,

00:00:58.253 --> 00:00:59.560
"leave it out of focus," I said,

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.630
"and I'll go, 'That's what she said.'"

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:04.330
And he says, "I don't, can't believe

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.870
"you made all that music
with just his mouth."

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:06.703
And they come in,

00:01:06.703 --> 00:01:08.000
"that's what she said."

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.630
People missed the first two times.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.540
The third time of
viewing, then they saw it.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.380
It was pretty much wasted.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.500
In the sixties I made love to

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.500
many, many women, often outdoors
in the rain and the mud.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.120
It's possible a man slipped in.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.570
There'd be no way of knowing.

00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:29.897
Ba-da-boom!

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:33.610
John Krasinski, when we were doing,

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.410
we'd do the scenes, he suggested

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.210
we do it like a David Mamet play.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.250
If you notice that one scene,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.040
I think it's Survivor Man, but we're both

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.245
in each other's face, like just going,

00:01:41.245 --> 00:01:42.078
(rolling tongue)

00:01:42.078 --> 00:01:44.020
just rapid fire stuff, and it was so,

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.500
it turned out so much fun.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:53.320
I was at the trial when
Toby was up there testifying

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.570
with blood all over me, with the parents

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:59.970
of the victims and stuff,
bereaved, the press,

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:00.970
nobody noticed me.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:01.940
No one saw me there.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:04.020
No one paid any attention.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.560
They got the wrong guy.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.036
- [Director] So was Creed
the Scranton Strangler?

00:02:08.036 --> 00:02:10.536
(music stops)

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.170
- Next question please.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.960
Bert.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.660
Bert Jacobs.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.780
Really good worm guy out in Pennsylvania.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:27.480
Well, he was selling weapons grade drugs

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.320
to kids besides IDs, military weapons,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.390
he had a slave trade
trafficking thing going on,

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.830
there were so many things we
were gonna bring up, you know.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.030
His father was found out to be an alien.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.800
That I asked Creed the other day, I said,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.890
"did you really kill me?"

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.030
And he hemmed and hawed for a long time,

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.620
and uh, I really couldn't get,

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.441
I really haven't got a
straight answer out of him

00:02:54.441 --> 00:02:56.540
and any of my personalities
about this thing.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.600
It's a quandary to be very honest.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.450
Kept my trailer, kept all my wardrobe,

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.870
I kept some cameras, sound equipment.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.380
When I came over recently to
visit the old sound stage,

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.280
you know, they had, you know,
an indictment against me,

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.190
basically.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:16.190
So I really can't go back there anymore.

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:22.410
I was over in Romania for a while,

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:26.160
shooting this noir Western
called The Sister Brothers.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.350
I'll be going on tour
to promote my new album

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.130
While the Young Punks Dance.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.310
He'd probably escape,
obviously, right away

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.640
from the Scranton police,

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.280
so he's probably off under an assumed name

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.530
doing the same thing he always did:

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.330
fishing, living in Canada,
going back and forth, you know,

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.810
selling drugs, killing people.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.819
Just having a really good life.

00:03:51.819 --> 00:03:55.236
(upbeat music continues)

00:04:02.425 --> 00:04:04.655
(squeaking)

